# Read by Docker and by the harbora CLI, which match differently: Docker anchors a plain name at the root and needs **/ for any depth, while
# harbora matches a plain name as a folder at any depth and cannot match a **/ pattern against the files inside it. Each rule that must hold
# at any depth is therefore written both ways. Above all Storage: local runs keep the database and the ChatGPT browser profiles, with their
# sign-in cookies, under src/Loomi/Storage, and none of that may travel to a build server.
.git
**/bin
**/obj
**/node_modules
**/Storage
Storage
**/wwwroot/dist
.claude
.github
.impeccable
.vs
artifacts
backups
design-reference
docs
scripts
test-results
tests
.env
